MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DOS-PORT (patch 0101, Phase 10 Stage 2). Standard MIDI File parser +
tick-driven event scheduler + abstract MidiBackend interface +
shippable no-op MidiBackendStub concrete backend. Validates the
MIDI-routing infrastructure end-to-end without requiring real audio
hardware (WaveBlaster / OPL3 — Stage 3 / 4 work).

Selected when SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_BACKEND=midi-stub. SoundManager::
music() routes through MidiScheduler instead of Organya / OGG; per-
frame tick from SoundManager::runFade() advances scheduler position +
dispatches elapsed events to the bound backend. Pixtone SFX continues
on SB16 DAC unchanged (independent dispatch path).

NEW files (4):

  src/sound/MidiScheduler.{h,cpp} — singleton; SMF parser supporting
    SMF Format 0 / 1 with PPQ division, channel events (note on/off,
    CC, program change), tempo + end-of-track meta events; running-
    status decoding; multi-track merge with stable sort by abs_tick;
    skips aftertouch / pressure / pitch-bend / SysEx / non-tempo meta
    silently. Tick-driven dispatch with us-per-tick recompute on
    tempo change; loop-from-start at end-of-song.

  src/sound/MidiBackendStub.{h,cpp} — concrete no-op backend. All
    dispatch methods LOG_DEBUG narrate (silent in release builds where
    Logger.cpp:53 default level is INFO). on_song_start /
    on_song_stop fire LOG_INFO so the stub's lifecycle is visible in
    DEBUG.LOG. Stage 3 (slot 0102+) replaces this with WaveBlaster
    backend consuming SDL/0037+ MPU-401 helpers; Stage 4 (slot 0103+)
    with OPL3.

MODIFIED (5):

  src/Utils/diagnostic_timers.h — extend AudioBackend enum with
    midi_stub = 5.
  src/graphics/Renderer.cpp — backend_to_string() handles midi_stub
    case (renders as "midi-stub" in [audio-block ...] emit).
  src/sound/AudioBackend.cpp — selectBackendFromEnv() handles
    "midi-stub" env value; sets g_p10_audio_backend_active =
    midi_stub. Other invalid values still fall back to organya;
    recognized-values list extended in fallback log.
  src/sound/SoundManager.h + .cpp — wire MidiScheduler into music
    dispatch:
      - init(): when backend == midi_stub, install MidiBackendStub
        on the singleton MidiScheduler
      - music(songno, resume): route via _start_mid_track when MIDI
        backend active; the existing Organya / OGG branches fire only
        on non-MIDI backends
      - enableMusic(newstate): MIDI-backend branch handles music-
        enabled toggle through MidiScheduler::start / stop
      - runFade(): per-frame tick driver; calls MidiScheduler::tick
        when MIDI backend active (return-early); Organya / OGG fade
        path unchanged otherwise
      - _start_mid_track(songno, resume) — NEW private helper;
        resolves data/midi/<trackname>.mid via ResourceManager +
        existing _music_names[] lookup; calls MidiScheduler::load +
        start. Missing files LOG_WARN + degrade gracefully (music
        slot stays silent; SFX continues — runtime-error fallback
        path per Stage 1.5 Stage 2 simplification).

Smoke (DOSBox-X-fast cpu=auto, mounted from build/stage):

  DEFAULT (AUDIO_BACKEND unset → organya): 110+ flips at title;
    "audio backend: auto → organya"; no crashes; regression PASS.

  AUDIO_BACKEND=midi-stub: 660+ flips at title + intro attract;
    "audio backend: midi-stub (Phase 10 Stage 2 — MidiScheduler...)";
    "Sound system: MidiScheduler armed with MidiBackendStub";
    parsed real Cave Story track end-to-end:
      "MidiScheduler::load: parsed 'data/midi/curly.mid'
       = 5684 events at 480 PPQ"
    backend dispatched: "midi-stub: on_song_start"
    no crashes / hangs / fatal markers / abort signals.

  Both modes show the binary launches, reaches title screen,
  continues rendering, and respects backend selection.

  Quality gates per team-lead 2026-05-06 dispatch:
    1. ✓ DOSBox-X smoke for AUDIO_BACKEND=midi-stub: launches,
       reaches title, gameplay; no crash, no hang.
    2. ✓ AUDIO_BACKEND=organya unchanged (regression).
    3. ✓ Patch applies cleanly on top of nxengine-evo/0100.
    4. ✓ strings-grep verifies binary contains MidiScheduler /
       MidiBackendStub / midi-stub class names + log strings.
    5. ✓ CWSDPMI launches (DOSBox-X smoke completes; CWSDPMI is
       loaded via the launcher's MOUNT D vendor/cwsdpmi pattern).

